cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use brotkit in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "brotkit: GPU-accelerated, SymPy-driven fractal rendering for notebooks"
abstract: >-
  brotkit separates iterating a fractal formula from colouring the result. Formulas are
  written in SymPy, differentiated and code-generated into fused Numba kernels for the CPU
  or GPU, and renders produce data layers that can be recoloured, saved and animated without
  re-iterating.
authors:
  - family-names: "O'Brien"
    given-names: "Eoin"
repository-code: "https://github.com/eoin-obrien/brotkit"
license: BSD-3-Clause
keywords:
  - fractal
  - mandelbrot
  - julia set
  - buddhabrot
  - sympy
  - numba
  - cuda
  - jupyter
